Go , Gin (HTTP framework) , GORM (ORM) , PostgreSQL

open PowerShell as an administrator 

1. choco install go or choco install golang
2. go version  // output=>  go version go1.25.6 windows/amd64
3. Verify Go path manually (if still not working)
Run this to check if Go exists:
dir "C:\Program Files\Go\bin"


STEP 1: Create project folder
mkdir go-gin-gorm-crud
cd go-gin-gorm-crud

STEP 2: Initialize Go module (VERY IMPORTANT)
This tells Go how to manage dependencies.
go mod init github.com/piyush/go-gin-gorm-crud

This creates:
go.mod

STEP 3: Install required libraries
go get -u github.com/gin-gonic/gin
go get -u gorm.io/gorm
go get -u gorm.io/driver/postgres

// These are now tracked in go.mod


STEP 4: Project structure

go-gin-gorm-crud/
│── main.go
│
├── config/
│   └── database.go
│
├── models/
│   └── user.go
│
├── controllers/
│   └── user_controller.go
│
├── routes/
│   └── routes.go
│
└── go.mod


STEP 5: PostgreSQL setup

Create database:
CREATE DATABASE go_crud;


STEP 6: Database connection (GORM)
📄 config/database.go


STEP 7: Create Model (Table)
📄 models/user.go

STEP 8: Auto-migrate table
📄 main.go

STEP 9: Controller (CRUD logic)
📄 controllers/user_controller.go


STEP 10: Routes
📄 routes/routes.go


STEP 11: Run the project
go run main.go




